.TH PMSET 1 "November 2026" "pmset 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
pmset \- manipulate power management settings on Linux and Omarchy
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B pmset
.RB [ \-a " | " \-b " | " \-c ]
.RI [ setting " " value ] ...
.BI "pmset \-g [" option "]"
.B pmset
.RB [ displaysleepnow | sleepnow | lock | touch | noidle | boot ]
.B pmset [\-h | \-\-help]
.B pmset [\-V | \-\-version]
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B pmset
is a Linux/Omarchy workalike for the macOS
.BR pmset (1)
command.  It implements the settings and actions that have a clear equivalent
on Linux, using the kernel, systemd-logind, and the Omarchy shell directly.
.PP
Settings are changed immediately.  Changing
.BR sleep ,
.BR lidwake ,
or
.B womp
requires root.  Changing
.B displaysleep
edits the invoking user's Omarchy configuration and does not require root;
when run through
.BR sudo ,
the user named by
.B SUDO_USER
is used.
.PP
The
.BR \-a ,
.BR \-b ,
and
.B \-c
flags are accepted for compatibility.  Linux settings are system-wide, so all
three apply to every power source.
.SH SETTINGS
Values for
.B displaysleep
and
.B sleep
are in minutes.  Fractional minutes are accepted and stored with second
precision.  A value of
.B 0
disables the timer.
.TP
.BI displaysleep " " N
Set the display idle timeout in the Omarchy shell configuration
.RI ( idle.screensaver
in
.IR ~/.config/omarchy/shell.json ).
The lock-screen timeout
.RI ( idle.lock )
is left unchanged.
.B dim
is accepted as a deprecated alias.
.TP
.BI sleep " " N
Suspend the system after
.I N
idle minutes by writing
.B IdleAction=suspend
and
.B IdleActionSec=Nmin
to
.IR /etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/99-pmset.conf .
A value of 0 writes
.BR IdleAction=ignore .
.TP
.BI lidwake " " 0|1
When set to 1, closing the lid suspends the system
.RB ( HandleLidSwitch=suspend
and
.BR HandleLidSwitchExternalPower=suspend ).
When set to 0, lid close is ignored.
.TP
.BI womp " " 0|1
Enable or disable Wake-on-LAN magic-packet wakeups on every interface that
supports them, using the kernel
.B SIOCETHTOOL
ioctl.
.TP
.BI disksleep " " N
Not supported.  ATA and NVMe devices do not share a reliable spindown interface.
.TP
.BI hibernatemode " " N
Not supported.  Use
.B omarchy hibernation setup
instead.
.SH GETTING
.TP
.B pmset \-g
.TQ
.B pmset \-g live
Show the settings currently in use.
.TP
.B pmset \-g custom
Show the settings with a note that they are system-wide.
.TP
.B pmset \-g cap
Show detected capabilities: battery, AC adapter, backlight, lid switch,
suspend, hibernate, and Wake-on-LAN.
.TP
.B pmset \-g batt
Show the current power source and battery state from
.IR /sys/class/power_supply .
.TP
.B pmset \-g ps
Show every battery and AC/USB power supply.
.TP
.B pmset \-g ac
.TQ
.B pmset \-g adapter
Show AC and USB supplies.
.TP
.B pmset \-g assertions
Show systemd inhibitors that block idle or sleep, using
.BR "systemd-inhibit --list" .
.TP
.B pmset \-g everything
Show settings, capabilities, battery state, and assertions.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B displaysleepnow
Turn the display off with Hyprland DPMS.  The session and compositor keep
running.  A short-lived Hyprland guard disables key-press wakeups until the
Enter key that started the command is released, then restores the original
setting; this is event-driven, so blanking is not delayed.  Restore the display
with
.B omarchy system wake
or
.BR "omarchy brightness display on" .
.TP
.B sleepnow
Suspend the system with
.B loginctl suspend
or, if loginctl is unavailable,
.BR "systemctl suspend" .
.TP
.B lock
Lock the session with
.B omarchy system lock
or, if Omarchy is unavailable,
.BR "loginctl lock-session" .
.TP
.B touch
Re-read settings.  This is a no-op because settings are read from the live
system on every invocation.
.TP
.B noidle
Hold a
.B "systemd-inhibit --what=idle:sleep"
block inhibitor until interrupted.  On macOS this command is deprecated in
favor of
.BR caffeinate (8);
systemd inhibitors fill the same role on Linux.
.TP
.B boot
No-op.  Linux has no equivalent of the Darwin boot-complete notification.
.SH EXAMPLES
Set the display timeout to 5 minutes and the idle suspend timeout to 30
minutes:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pmset \-a displaysleep 5 sleep 30
.RE
.fi
.PP
Turn the display off immediately:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pmset displaysleepnow
.RE
.fi
.PP
Show battery state:
.PP
.nf
.RS
pmset \-g batt
.RE
.fi
.SH NOTES
.B pmset sleep
configures logind's idle action.  logind only acts on it when the session
publishes an idle hint.  Omarchy's Hyprland/uwsm session does not currently set
one, so the idle timer may not fire there.  Use
.B pmset sleepnow
for an immediate suspend, or a compositor idle daemon such as
.BR hypridle (1)
if an automatic idle suspend is required.
.SH LIMITATIONS
The following macOS settings have no reliable Linux equivalent and are
rejected:
.BR disksleep ,
.BR spindown ,
.BR hibernatemode ,
.BR hibernatefile ,
.BR autorestart ,
.BR halfdim ,
.BR lessbright ,
.BR acwake ,
.BR ring ,
.BR sms ,
.BR ttyskeepawake ,
.BR destroyfvkeyonstandby ,
.BR autopoweroff ,
and
.BR autopoweroffdelay .
.PP
Scheduled and repeating power events
.RB ( schedule ,
.BR repeat ,
.B relative )
are not implemented.  Use systemd timers or
.BR rtcwake (8).
.PP
UPS emergency thresholds
.RB ( \-u ,
.BR haltlevel ,
.BR haltafter ,
.B haltremain )
are not implemented; use UPower or NUT.
.PP
The
.BR \-g
options
.BR sched ,
.BR ups ,
.BR pslog ,
.BR rawlog ,
.BR therm ,
.BR thermlog ,
.BR sysload ,
.BR sysloadlog ,
.BR uuid ,
.BR uuidlog ,
.BR history ,
.BR historydetailed ,
.BR powerstate ,
.BR powerstatelog ,
.BR stats ,
and
.B systemstate
are not supported.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.config/omarchy/shell.json
Omarchy shell configuration.  The
.B idle.screensaver
value is the display idle timeout.
.TP
.I /etc/systemd/logind.conf.d/99-pmset.conf
Generated by
.BR pmset .
Holds idle-suspend and lid-switch settings.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR loginctl (1),
.BR logind.conf (5),
.BR systemd-inhibit (1),
.BR rtcwake (8),
.BR brightnessctl (1),
.BR hyprctl (1)
